WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:12.639
Jerusalem has seen some of its worst violence
in years.

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:22.350
It began with protests in the usually quiet
neighborhood of Sheikh Jarrah in East Jerusalem.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:28.580
The demonstrations spread to other parts of
the city - including to the Al Aqsa mosque,

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.739
one of the holiest sites in Islam.

00:00:31.739 --> 00:00:37.260
Heavy-handed policing fueled anger as tensions
escalated.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:44.580
Many see this as the spark that triggered
one of the deadliest episodes of the Israeli-Palestinian

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.340
conflict in recent history.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:58.730
But tensions are still simmering over the
planned eviction of Palestinian families in

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.899
Sheikh Jarrah.

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:05.339
So what’s going on there and why is it important?

00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:12.300
Sheikh Jarrah is a Palestinian neighborhood
in Israeli-occupied East Jerusalem.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:19.530
Most of the people who live here are Palestinians
- but in the past few years, Jewish settlers

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:24.300
have moved into some properties.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:30.350
Protests flared recently over plans to evict
Palestinian families to make way for more

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.350
settlers.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:37.590
It’s all part of a long-running dispute
over the ownership of the land and who has

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.500
the right to live there.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:48.030
To understand why, we have to go back to the
Arab-Israeli war of 1948, after Israel declared

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.400
its independence.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:57.140
The conflict displaced some 750,000 Palestinians.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:03.540
Some of them were later resettled in Sheikh
Jarrah as part of a Jordanian project funded

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.320
by the United Nations.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:12.360
Some of the land had previously been owned
by two Jewish associations.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:20.970
In 1967, Israel effectively annexed East Jerusalem
- including Sheikh Jarrah.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:27.620
Israel views Jerusalem as its ‘unified,
eternal’ capital and denies that East Jerusalem

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.890
is occupied.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:36.100
But with it under Israeli control, Jewish
settlers started launching legal challenges

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:39.319
to claim ownership of the land.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:48.490
"So in 1950 Israel legislated a law, the Absentee
property law that says that Palestinians cannot

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:51.230
return to their properties in Israel.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:59.190
In 1970 after Israel annexed East Jerusalem
the Knesset legislated that Jews can return

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:06.670
to properties so this is the basis or the
discriminatory basis of all the court cases

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:12.840
of evictions that we are seeing in Sheikh
Jarrah &amp; Silwan that settler manage to take

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:19.400
out the ownership from before 1948 and now
they are suing the Palestinians out of their

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.520
homes.”

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:26.709
This is at the heart of the conflict in Sheikh
Jarrah.

00:03:26.709 --> 00:03:32.760
Seven families are facing eviction to make
way for Jewish settlers - with several more

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.400
in the middle of court proceedings.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:41.050
The land belongs to Jews for almost a hundred
years.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:47.400
Jews lived there, and Jews own the land since
then.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.400
Nothing has changed.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.980
What has changed now is that suddenly the
Arabs decided that they are the owners of

00:03:52.980 --> 00:04:01.380
the land and they don't want to accept the
Jewish ownership."

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:07.220
The families, though, say the laws are discriminatory
- and that it’s not a real-estate dispute,

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.970
but a case of forced expulsion.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.700
“And this is our life.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:18.419
We are the owners of the land, the Palestinians,
who have legally lived here, with legal proof

00:04:18.419 --> 00:04:20.959
for everything [related to living here].

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:29.099
And here they are, the settlers have come,
they occupied our houses and they want to

00:04:29.099 --> 00:04:31.659
occupy what remains of the neighborhood.”

00:04:31.659 --> 00:04:34.780
This isn’t just happening in Sheikh Jarrah.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:41.250
There are dozens more cases in another East
Jerusalem neighborhood, Silwan.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:49.379
According to international law, Israel can’t
confiscate property in an occupied territory.

00:04:49.379 --> 00:04:55.989
The UN has called for a halt to the evictions,
saying they may amount to a war crime.

